:: 2.1 {"position":"675,1350","size":"100,100"}

<span style="color: #73AB76;">Kiran:</span> Hello! I'm Kiran. Thanks for meeting with me.


[["Hello! I'm a volunteer! What brings you in today?"|2.21]]
[["Are you lost?"|2.3]]


<!-- CHARACTER IMAGE -->
<img src="https://i.imgur.com/BBkC4Fk.png"
     style="
       position: fixed;
       bottom: 0;
       right: -200px;
       width: 900px;
       height: auto;
       z-index: 10;
     ">



:: 2.12122222 {"position":"850,1875","size":"100,100"}
Great choice! You validate Kiran's feelings while helping them separate their identity from their accomplishments. This reflects the chapter's concept of Being vs. Doing, which emphasizes that failure in something we do does not define who we are.

<!-- NEXT BUTTON -->
<div style="
  position: fixed;
  bottom: 40px;
  left: 40px;
  z-index: 1000;
">
[[Next|2.212121212]]
</div>


:: 2.12134434322 {"position":"325,2300","size":"100,100"}
Great choice! You encourage Kiran to view rejection as an opportunity for learning rather than a reflection of her abilities. This demonstrates Failure Reframing, which involves reflecting on setbacks, identifying lessons, and using those insights to guide future actions.

<div style="
  position: fixed;
  bottom: 40px;
  left: 40px;
  z-index: 1000;
">
[[Next|wfwfwwfw]]
</div>


:: 2.21 {"position":"675,1500","size":"100,100"}
<span style="color: #73AB76;">Kiran:</span> I booked this appointment because I really don't know what to do anymore...

I recently applied for a research position that I was really excited about. I spent weeks preparing my application, but I just found out that I didn't get it.

I know rejection is normal, but I can't help feeling like I wasn't good enough.

[["I see this position was important to you"|2.212]]

<!-- CHARACTER IMAGE -->
<img src="https://i.imgur.com/BBkC4Fk.png"
     style="
       position: fixed;
       bottom: 0;
       right: -200px;
       width: 900px;
       height: auto;
       z-index: 10;
     ">


:: 2.211112 {"position":"850,1700","size":"100,100"}
<span style="color: #73AB76;">Kiran:</span> I guess, but I don't know if I'll get another opportunity.

[[I understand|2.213]]

<!-- CHARACTER IMAGE -->
<img src="https://i.imgur.com/BBkC4Fk.png"
     style="
       position: fixed;
       bottom: 0;
       right: -200px;
       width: 900px;
       height: auto;
       z-index: 10;
     ">


:: 2.212 {"position":"675,1650","size":"100,100"}
<span style="color: #73AB76;">Kiran:</span> Yes... it was. I thought it would help me get into graduate school. I've worked so hard these past four years, and I feel like everything was leading up to this. Now I'm worried I've ruined my chances.

[["It sounds like you've put a lot of effort into this, so I can understand why you're disappointed. It must be stressful feeling like your future depends on this opportunity."|2.213]]

[["I'm sure you'll find another research position! You have good grades, so I wouldn't worry too much about it."|2.211112]]

[["Rejection is a normal part of life. You can't let one unsuccessful application affect you this much."|2.2221222]]




:: 2.212121212 {"position":"700,2075","size":"100,100"}
[["What do you think you could learn from this experience"|2.22212121]]
[["Maybe you're not fit for the position...|2.232323223222]]


:: 2.213 {"position":"700,1825","size":"100,100"}
<span style="color: #73AB76;">Kiran:</span> I feel like I've put so much pressure on myself to succeed. 

I guess I've always thought of myself as someone who's academically successful. When I don't achieve something, it feels like I've failed as a person, not just at one application.

[["You're being too hard on yourself. It's just one rejection, and you've accomplished so much already. You shouldn't let it bother you."|2.2222121]]

[["That sounds really difficult, especially when academics have been such a big part of your life. But not getting this position doesn't take away from everything you've accomplished or who you are as a person."|2.12122222]]




:: 2.22212121 {"position":"525,2225","size":"100,100"}
<span style="color: #73AB76;">Kiran:</span> I haven't really thought about it that way. I guess I could ask for feedback on my application. Maybe there are things I could improve for next time.

[["That's a really thoughtful way to look at it! Even though the outcome wasn't what you hoped for, asking for feedback could help you understand what worked and what you might do differently next time."|2.12134434322]]

[["Definitely! You should ask for feedback and make sure you fix all the mistakes in your application so you don't get rejected again."|232323.2222]]


<!-- CHARACTER IMAGE -->
<img src="https://i.imgur.com/BBkC4Fk.png"
     style="
       position: fixed;
       bottom: 0;
       right: 0px;
       width: 900px;
       height: auto;
       z-index: 10;
       transform: scaleX(-1);
     ">


